With a paid seat, any purpose is a permitted purpose.  With a free seat, only a noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose for a free seat, except as limited by [Government Institutions](#government-institutions).

## Government Institutions

Notwithstanding any other section of these terms, use by or for a government institution is **not** a permitted purpose for a free seat, whether or not that use would otherwise be noncommercial and whether or not it would otherwise qualify under [Personal Uses](#personal-uses).  A government institution needs a paid seat for each developer.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for the benefit of public knowledge, personal study, private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or religious observance, without any anticipated commercial application, is use for a permitted purpose.

## Noncommercial Organizations

Use by any charitable organization, educational institution, public research organization, public safety or health organization, or environmental protection organization is use for a permitted purpose regardless of the source of funding or obligations resulting from the funding.  This holds even where such an organization is publicly funded, publicly run, or otherwise part of a government institution.

