The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these terms.

The **software** is the software the licensor makes available under these terms, in every form the licensor makes it available - source code, compiled unit files (`.dcu`), executable files (including `Autopilot.Mcp.exe`), packages, and documentation - together with any changed or derived version of any part of it.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or other kind of organization that you work for, plus all organizations that have control over, are under the control of, or are under common control with that organization.  **Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or the power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract, or otherwise.  Control can be direct or indirect.

**A government institution** is any national, federal, state, regional, provincial, municipal, or local government, and any agency, department, ministry, authority, court, armed force, public administration, or state-owned enterprise of such a government, as well as any intergovernmental or supranational organization.  An organization covered by [Noncommercial Organizations](#noncommercial-organizations) is not a government institution for the purpose of these terms, even when it is publicly funded or publicly run.

